ad broken the 800 world record with 1:44.3 in Christchurch in 1962. Before Tokyo he had also claimed the world mile record. In the Tokyo final, the first lap was led by Kenyan " [:a {:href "/athletes/72777"} "Wilson Kiprugut"] " in 52.0. Snell was boxed at the bell, but moved out into lane three on the backstretch and blew by everybody. On the final curve, Jamaican " [:a {:href "/athletes/72297"} "George Kerr"] " stayed close but could not never gain on Snell. At the start of the homestretch Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/66010"} "Bill Crothers"] " pulled ahead of Kerr and would win the silver medal, Kiprugut getting bronze. Kiprugut became the first Kenyan runner to win an Olympic medal.Snell defended his 800 metres title, following in the footsteps of " [:a {:href "/athletes/69262"} "Douglas Lowe"] " (1924-28) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/79185"} "Mal Whitfield"] " (1948-52). A few days later he would add the 1,500, also achieving the 800/1,500 double."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "466"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/74357"} "Peter Snell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "1:49.0 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "1:46.9 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:45.1 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "57"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/66010"} "Bill Crothers"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [